@* shadcn’s own: small, an icon tinted with the destructive colour above the question, and the
   destructive recipe on the action rather than on the trigger — the colour belongs to the thing
   that does the damage, not to the thing that opens the question.

   Variant on the button, not a hand-built class string: AlertDialogAction has the parameter, and
   passing ButtonVariants.Of(...) as a Class was building the same thing twice. *@
<AlertDialogTrigger Target="ad-destructive" Variant="destructive">Delete Chat</AlertDialogTrigger>

<AlertDialog Id="ad-destructive" Size="sm">
    <AlertDialogHeader>
        <AlertDialogMedia aria-hidden="true"
                          Class="bg-destructive/10 text-destructive dark:bg-destructive/20">
            <Icon Name="trash-2" />
        </AlertDialogMedia>
        <AlertDialogTitle>Delete chat?</AlertDialogTitle>
        <AlertDialogDescription>
            This permanently deletes the conversation. Anything it remembered goes with it.
        </AlertDialogDescription>
    </AlertDialogHeader>
    <AlertDialogFooter>
        <AlertDialogCancel Variant="outline">Cancel</AlertDialogCancel>
        <AlertDialogAction Variant="destructive">Delete</AlertDialogAction>
    </AlertDialogFooter>
</AlertDialog>
